{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade","id":635621,"title":"Wraiths in Vampire the Masquerade","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-22T05:19:23-07:00","id":635621,"title":"Wraiths in Vampire the Masquerade","content":"My friends play a little old wod once in a while. We almost never get to do it. But when we do, it is usually a mix between either everyone is a vampire or you can be mage,wolf or vamp etc....<br /> <br /> He wants to do another game with mummy's which I know nothing about and wraiths. <br /> <br /> Which means we have vampires, werewolves, changlings, mages, hunters (somehow?) and demons to choose from.....but I REALLY like the story and fluff from wraith and I want to try it sometime. But I have a few questions.<br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Do I HAVE to look exactly human being like? Or can I just be a vaugly human shape of mist with a somewhat human looking face?<br /> 2. Can I float everywhere? I really dislike the idea of being forced to gravity when I am completely ethereal.<br /> <br /> <br /> 3. The important question is how do I make a wraith work in the skinlands world? What if I don't WANT to dwell in the shadow lands or just keep it as a second home? What if some other super rich wraith somehow succumbed to his shadow and I just happend to be in the area when he went to oblivion....looked around and said this is mine now and his ghost mansion was mine and no one else in the area for whatever their own reasons just accepted the idea.....so I got bored and head out to the real world?<br /> <br /> How would I make that work and how would my GM be able to juggle my shadow and my stuff while me being able to keep myself in this place? Especially if I wanted to be all.. oooouuuhh.....OOOooooHHHHHH!! I am a ghoooooosttt!! and then have people running out of the room as the walls leak blood and hot dog rat swarms out from the ceilings with floating furnature flying around the room? <br /> <br /> <br /> I wanna use wraiths in the real world and hang with vampires, witches and werewolves.....so how do I make that happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7409-veil","name":"veil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T08:06:44-07:00","id":635811,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. Do I HAVE to look exactly human being like? Or can I just be a vaugly human shape of mist with a somewhat human looking face? </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Well, mostly no, with a little yes. In the Underworld (or if you cross the Shroud via Inhabit), you don\u2019t have to look too human, but you\u2019ll still be tangible.*1</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can I float everywhere? I really dislike the idea of being forced to gravity when I am completely ethereal. </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Not so much with the floating. Check out the Rule of Ouch on page 232 in WtO Second Edition. You might be able to talk your ST into some narrative leeway.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">3. The important question is how do I make a wraith work in the skinlands world? What if I don't WANT to dwell in the shadow lands or just keep it as a second home?</span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Without additional Arcanoi, your character can observe the Skinlands </span><i>through</i><span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\"> the Shadowlands. Depending on the level of the Shroud, some humans might catch a glimpse (giving you that hazy appearance you mentioned earlier), but it\u2019s sort of one-way thing. There\u2019s a few Arcanoi that help with interaction*2</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What if some other super rich wraith somehow succumbed to his shadow and I just happend to be in the area when he went to oblivion....looked around and said this is mine now and his ghost mansion was mine and no one else in the area for whatever their own reasons just accepted the idea.....so I got bored and head out to the real world? </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">I don\u2019t see why couldn\u2019t have a Haunt that\u2019s a mansion. You\u2019d have to work that out with your ST. It doesn\u2019t even have to belong to someone else; maybe it was yours when you were alive.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How would I make that work and how would my GM be able to juggle my shadow and my stuff while me being able to keep myself in this place? Especially if I wanted to be all.. oooouuuhh.....OOOooooHHHHHH!! I am a ghoooooosttt!! and then have people running out of the room as the walls leak blood and hot dog rat swarms out from the ceilings with floating furnature flying around the room? </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">It sounds like you want your character\u2019s day job to be \u201cspookmaster for a haunted mansion\u201d then hang out with other supernatural critters when you\u2019re off the clock? Check out the Background Haunt and the Arcanos Pandemonium.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Using the Rules As Written (RAW), the other characters will need some sort of powers to interact with you. Vampires need some Necromancy (maybe Auspex or Thaumaturgy), I think sluagh can see wraiths, Spirit Sphere for mages, and I\u2019m not sure about the other Splats. Unless, of course, your ST wants to hand-wave it and rule that all supernatural critters can see wraiths (which wouldn\u2019t be a bad way to go for a game like this).</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wanna use wraiths in the real world and hang with vampires, witches and werewolves.....so how do I make that happen? </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Are you familiar with the Risen?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">*1 However, I think there was a Merit and/or Flaw in the Wraith Player\u2019s Guide.<br /> <br /> *2 Off the top of head, Outrage, Pandemonium, and Inhabit.</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T11:24:28-07:00","id":636094,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the second dot in Argos allow for floating/gliding?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T13:58:27-07:00","id":636251,"title":"","content":"Oh man! I just found a 5 dot power in one of these things that will allow me to x-form into the girl from the ring movie from the evil within game! You know...the screaming, multiarmed adult one that is like...UBER FREAKING SCARY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7409-veil","name":"veil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T14:15:50-07:00","id":636268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>veil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=636251#post636251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man! I just found a 5 dot power in one of these things that will allow me to x-form into the girl from the ring movie from the evil within game! You know...the screaming, multiarmed adult one that is like...UBER FREAKING SCARY.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean Moliate? That combined with the Omnidexterous merit can make that real easy to accomplish. In general, most of the Arcanoi can allow you to emulate near perfectly some sort of ghost from a movie or game. Got a thing for dreams like Freddy Krueger? Easy. Phantasm has got you covered. Want to be more like Sam Wheat from Ghost? Outrage and a pinch of Puppetry. What about those crazy spirits in Poltergeist? Pandemonium for the main course and a whole host of other Arcanoi to spice things up. Wanna pull a Jacob Marley and warn your old friend that they are going to regret their choices in life? Embody is your power. Want to mess around with your appearance like Adam and Barbara did in Beetlejuice? Moliate, as mentioned above. The sky is practically the limit when it comes to these abilities, and it's one of the main things that draws me to Wraith (to say nothing of the whole Shadow aspect).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T14:33:43-07:00","id":636277,"title":"","content":"Quick responses:<br /> <br /> Floating: Get some dots in Argos. Problem Solved.<br /> <br /> Interacting with the Skinlands: Embody:4 (incorrectly named &quot;Life-in-Death&quot;, which should be the level 5 power, while *that* name, &quot;Materialize&quot; should be the 4th, but anywho -- that's an old discussion...) can let a wraith (with enough Pathos and successes) remain in a material form for even hours at a time. This is uncommon, true, but I played a character who started out the gate with Embody:4 -- he simply refused to let being dead get in the way of his plans/goals, and although he looked &quot;unwell/somewhat unnaturally pale&quot;, we could still get certain business done and be with people for certain periods of time (he'd also &quot;disappear&quot; for days or even weeks on end, but much of that was covered by down time to represent his recovering his strength so he could continue doing his Skinland business).<br /> <br /> Appearance/Mein: you *can* use Moliate to alter your features and even Materialize with said changes -- you just can't be in a radically inhuman form. That is, you can use it took look somewhat inhuman, or even look like someone else, but you can have multiple limbs, look shockingly horrifying (by WoD standards), or the like.<br /> <br /> Haunts/Shadowland possessions: Almost anything is *possible*, but the thing to keep in mind is that the more you have, the more you have to protect/guard from others -- good Haunts are hard to come by, as are Relics/Artifacts and similar, so if you have a mansion (as a Haunt linked to the Skinlands, or a removed one in the Shadowlands), then it may well come to the attention of other wraiths who will want to take possession of it, themselves.... Be careful what you wish for....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T17:04:31-07:00","id":636467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=636277#post636277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is uncommon, true, but I played a character who started out the gate with Embody:4 -- he simply refused to let being dead get in the way of his plans/goals, and although he looked &quot;unwell/somewhat unnaturally pale&quot;,</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally took the &quot;look like how you do as a dead person&quot; approach with the level 4 Embody art. Might be considered a flaw, but it can be great for frightening others (especially if you died in a particularly mangled, bloody way) or just being &quot;cool&quot;. Can present some obstacles which lends itself well to role playing. A lover reappearing after a year of being dead (wedding anniversary cliche FTW) with all the bits of gore and charred flesh she had when she died in that horrible fire can present serious issues from the still living spouse. I mean, they're dead, but they also look like <i>that</i>. Simply awesome, and even gives more motivation on the wraith's part to master the Embody Arcanos so they can look 100% normal again. Best part is this has a varying degree of issues, since one person might have died from asphyxiation, a second from gunshot wounds, and the other from being eaten by a gator. Three very, very different levels of violence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7234-the-dreamweaver","name":"The Dreamweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7234_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T03:38:59-07:00","id":636863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nazfool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=635811#post635811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">Are you familiar with the Risen?</span><br /> ]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I tried looking for the risen in the book but only found one sentence mention of it. So what do? What are rules and stuff for it? I don't really know much about wraith since the book I got is still new to me. I read a page or two of its fluff and fell in love with the flavor of it and the aspect of being a spookster! As long as I can be all floating around, make the walls drip blood while at the same time a dead body that some werewolves are eating sits up, pulls off its face and its eyes jut out their socts as it shakes its head while screaming like the crypt keeper from tales from the crypt and then finally I pop out of the ground in a bloody screaming explosion like this girl!<br /> <br /> <br /> SKIP TO 17:51 on this video.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTlzeHc-EYc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTlzeHc-EYc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTlzeHc-EYc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dTlzeHc-EYc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> ...I wanna do THAT as my finisher and send all dem werewolves out of da room screaming like little human girls!<br /> <br /> <br /> BUT from all the suggestions. It looks like I got my problems solved! Cool! Can't wait to make an explosion of screaming blood mutated ring girl action!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7409,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7409-veil","user":"veil","date":". 08-23-2015, 06:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7409-veil","name":"veil","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T08:42:32-07:00","id":637052,"title":"","content":"The Risen have their own book within WtO called... well <i>The Risen</i>. They are wraiths that have struck a deal with Shadows and have managed to return their corpses. They are pretty formidable in that state if they can achieve it. Plus it provides them with several new Arcanoi and a few vampire Disciplines. Of course a number of Arcanoi are unusable or restricted in that state.<br /> <br /> You can find a basic overview of the Risen <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Risen\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> And the book for purchase as a PDF <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/250/The-Risen?it=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> When it comes to WtO crossovers, the Risen that are probably the best bet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-29T18:58:23-07:00","id":740538,"title":"","content":"Risen are pretty metal. They're basically half vampire, half ghosts with none of the draw backs. Also they have strength that makes Vampires question their judgement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T15:55:36-08:00","id":752333,"title":"","content":"following along with this topic. i have recently started a game of masquerade, on V20 and i took the flaw of haunted, however i also have a resources of 4 and the large house i start with is quite large and nice, but due to my flaw it is haunted by a particularly nasty wraith, which also killed my sire who i loved dearly. now my problem is i want to clear the house of this entity. is there a way for a vampire to, for lack of a better word, &quot;kill&quot; a wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9083-pandemonix","name":"Pandemonix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-03T19:40:46-08:00","id":752848,"title":"","content":"You could probably manage something with Necromancy. If you can't find someone to help with that, you'll need to resort to other measures to deal with the wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T01:05:19-08:00","id":753358,"title":"","content":"You might also be able to placate the wraith if you can help it resolve its Passions or Fetters. It's a good idea to try to find out why the wraith is hanging around and why it's angry. It could just be a spectre, in which case it needs to be destroyed. But if it's just a wraith with a few issues, it could prove a useful ally if you help it. <br /> <br /> Wraiths are also incredibly hardy. They don't 'die' easily. You usually have to reduce them from 10 permanent Corpus to zero, which is a hard thing to do, or have them otherwise taken care of across the Shroud (soulforged, Moliated, enslaved, etc).<br /> <br /> A necromancer might also exact quite a high price for destroying a wraith, since there are possible repercussions for her too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-04-2015, 04:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T17:36:52-08:00","id":757556,"title":"","content":"oooo very nice deatails, ok a little more knowledge. i dont know anything about wraiths personaly, but my storyteller used to play it alot in the 90's. i did catch a couple of details he didnt know he let on to. 1 this particular wraith didnt have to wait a year and a day before coming back. sooo im guesssing that might help you peeps with the knowledge understand what type of wraith we are dealing with, second when he was human i was human, my sire broke me out of an mental ward at a hospital. from there she had ghouled me and had me hunt 1 particular survivor of the hospital which i had fun hunting this guy down, (what can i say i enjoy a good hunt) but right as i caught him my sire killed him brutaly. and shortly after coming back he killed my sire.<br /> with what you guys have told me so far, it would seem my only recourse is to try and find a vamp with necromancy, because i dont think there would be a way my char would try to make peace with it.<br /> chances are if it has unresolved issues, then those are to kill me sooooo....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9083-pandemonix","name":"Pandemonix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T20:59:07-08:00","id":757875,"title":"","content":"Doesn't destroying a wraith's fetter plunge it into a harrowing in the Labyrinth that could conceivably destroy it, or at least remove it from interaction with the world of the living for an extended period? Might be worth researching exactly who the wraith was and what he could be hanging around for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T23:03:18-08:00","id":758071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=757875#post757875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't destroying a wraith's fetter plunge it into a harrowing in the Labyrinth that could conceivably destroy it, or at least remove it from interaction with the world of the living for an extended period? Might be worth researching exactly who the wraith was and what he could be hanging around for.</div> </div> </div> </div>It takes ten <i>failed</i> Harrowings to destroy a wraith. Destroying all of the wraith's Fetters is almost as good, preventing the wraith from getting anywhere <i>near</i> the living world . . . but that's probably not an option here. The vampire in question is probably one of those Fetters, and unlikely to accept suicide as an option. <br /> <br /> In the short term, blackmail is probably the best option. Find someone he really cares about (beyond being a Fetter) - their son, wife, etc - and arrange to have them tortured to death in the most horrible fashion you can think of, should something happen to him. Sort of a vampiric &quot;dead man's switch&quot;. <br /> <br /> That'll be very hard on his Humanity, but it'll work as a stop gap solution. And if this wraith is powerful enough <i>already</i> to kill someone in the living world, said vampire desperately needs one.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T07:00:06-08:00","id":758596,"title":"","content":"You could also get a blood sorcerer to enact the ritual Ward Against Ghosts. A temporary solution, but one that might suffice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T23:01:33-08:00","id":759768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=758071#post758071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It takes ten <i>failed</i> Harrowings to destroy a wraith. Destroying all of the wraith's Fetters is almost as good, preventing the wraith from getting anywhere <i>near</i> the living world . . . but that's probably not an option here. The vampire in question is probably one of those Fetters, and unlikely to accept suicide as an option.<br /> <br /> In the short term, blackmail is probably the best option. Find someone he really cares about (beyond being a Fetter) - their son, wife, etc - and arrange to have them tortured to death in the most horrible fashion you can think of, should something happen to him. Sort of a vampiric &quot;dead man's switch&quot;.<br /> <br /> That'll be very hard on his Humanity, but it'll work as a stop gap solution. And if this wraith is powerful enough <i>already</i> to kill someone in the living world, said vampire desperately needs one.</div> </div> </div> </div>ok i havnt a clue on what a harrowing is, but as far as blackmail goes...ooooo man i love the way you think. thank youuuuuuuuuu soooooooo much. you are awesome!!!! ima blackmail a ghost","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9083-pandemonix","name":"Pandemonix","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T05:05:49-08:00","id":759905,"title":"","content":"A harrowing is what happens when a wraith is reduced to zero corpus (effectively health levels, but they work a bit differently). It involves a trip through a chaotic hellscape called the Tempest. It's not really relevant to Vampire under most circumstances, but what it means is that it takes a lot of effort to get rid of a wraith for good.<br /> <br /> Well, unless you can make contacts on the other side who will capture and soulforge the wraith into an ashtray for you. But that seems unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T08:52:00-08:00","id":760008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=759905#post759905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A harrowing is what happens when a wraith is reduced to zero corpus (effectively health levels, but they work a bit differently). It involves a trip through a chaotic hellscape called the Tempest. It's not really relevant to Vampire under most circumstances, but what it means is that it takes a lot of effort to get rid of a wraith for good.<br /> <br /> Well, unless you can make contacts on the other side who will capture and soulforge the wraith into an ashtray for you. But that seems unlikely.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that it's extremely unlikely for a vampire of any sort to know enough about Shadowland politics to get word to the right folks.... but this wraith seems like he's violating the Dictum Mortuum as written (though I'm sure he could argue that he's not, since a vampire isn't alive.... but how often does the Hierarchy do trials and such instead of having some legionnaires bust down the door and drag the perp off to the forges?) If the wraith in question gets too overt, his future might lie along the lines of becoming someone's doorstop.<br /> <br /> Actually... there MIGHT be a way to work with that. Though it would be more correlation that direct causation. Maybe he should hire/notify some of the celebrity ghost-hunters and have them come to investigate his lovely home. If the wraith pulled his shit on camera.... The Hierarchy might notice and then he'd end up as coinage or as a doorstop or Moliated into a screaming face on an Anacreon's latest party dress... The vamp might think he's just doing a spiritual &quot;fumigation&quot;, and he is... it's just not working the way he imagines it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":".  More Ideas 11-07-2015, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-07T15:43:07-08:00","id":760284,"title":"","content":"If Orpheus happens in your world, you could get someone from Orpheus to sort the ghost out. Perhaps using mortal pawns to avoid drawing attention to your own nature.<br /> <br /> There are lots of mortal mediums, as well, as per Mediums: Speakers with the Dead. Some of them might help (for a fee, but perhaps with fewer strings than a Giovanni deal).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-08T18:17:54-08:00","id":761094,"title":"","content":"I recall that at least in the Wraith 2nd Edition rules, all it takes is something like Occult 3 to perform folkloric warding ceremonies that will raise the Shroud of a home to one's Willpower rating. One of my characters had an Oprichniki gal Friday and after he got fed up with broken crockery and bleeding walls he used this method to give his townhouse a Shroud like spring break in Cabo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T08:27:15-08:00","id":762338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/635621-wraiths-in-vampire-the-masquerade?p=761094#post761094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recall that at least in the Wraith 2nd Edition rules, all it takes is something like Occult 3 to perform folkloric warding ceremonies that will raise the Shroud of a home to one's Willpower rating. One of my characters had an Oprichniki gal Friday and after he got fed up with broken crockery and bleeding walls he used this method to give his townhouse a Shroud like spring break in Cabo.</div> </div> </div> </div>A determined Haunter could just spend time to overcome the increased difficulties, though. The Shroud can't get higher than 10, so there's always at least a small chance of success.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}